# The credential of credential-broken.rel, with one more equation.
#
# The first row still puts both attributes on the same generator g,
# which is the shape a checklist would object to. It is still there.
# But the second equation pins a1 on g and a2 on k, so the incidence
# system now forces a1 = a2 = r = 0 and the statement is DETERMINED.
#
# So "reject any statement with a repeated base in a row" is not a
# sound rule: the shape it looks for occurs in sound statements.
# Compiler/NoChecklist.v proves this for every rule of that form,
# whatever shape it looks for.
secrets a1 a2 r
claims  a1 a2 r
eq  C   g  g  h
eq  D   g  k  1
